This package builds and runs Vampire, and the `vampire-worker` binary it
produces is Vampire with one extra translation unit (`worker/worker.cpp`) linked
in. Vampire's licence is a BSD 3-Clause licence, which permits that; anyone who
*distributes* such a binary has to carry Vampire's copyright notice and
disclaimer with it, and may not use the names of Vampire's authors to endorse
what they distribute. This repository does not distribute one -- it is built
where it is used.

    Vampire — https://github.com/vprover/vampire
    Built from https://github.com/Dragon-Hatcher/vampire-tactic-vampire, a fork
    carrying the changes that make a proof readable back: what each inference
    used its premises for, the substitutions it applied, and the steps
    clausification took.
    Vampire's licence is at https://vprover.github.io/license.html

Vampire's own build fetches two further components as submodules, and links both
into the binary:

    CaDiCaL — https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical
    MIT licence, Copyright (c) 2016-2021 Armin Biere, Johannes Kepler
    University Linz, Austria.

    VIRAS — https://github.com/joe-hauns/viras
    That repository carries no licence file and states no terms. It is used
    here as a part of Vampire's build, which declares it.

`Vampire/Preprocess.lean` follows lean-smt in how it reduces a goal to the
smallest query that states it. lean-smt is used under the Apache License 2.0.

    lean-smt — https://github.com/ufmg-smite/lean-smt
    Copyright (c) 2021-2026 by the authors listed in that project's AUTHORS file
    and their institutional affiliations.

